docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:138:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Ej28FXYapwJWArijAgKsL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse serde_json::{json, Value};\n2\tuse std::collections::HashSet;\n3\tuse std::path::PathBuf;\n4\tuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, Ordering};\n5\tuse std::sync::{Arc, OnceLock};\n6\tuse tokio::sync::Mutex;\n7\tuse tokio::sync::MutexGuard;\n8\t\n9\tuse lattice_core::embeddings::EmbeddingEngine;\n10\tuse lattice_core::graph::model::{CodeGraph, GraphNode};\n11\tuse lattice_core::indexer::Indexer;\n12\tuse lattice_core::intelligence::{\n13\t    diagnose_failure, expand_context, find_relevant_tests, find_stale_docs, get_backlinks,\n14\t    get_docs_capsule, get_outgoing_links, get_repo_playbook, get_working_set_context,\n15\t    impact_from_diff, plan_edit, prepare_change, summarize_subsystem, trace_scenario, BundleMode,\n16\t    DiffImpactReport, DocsTargetKind, ExpandContextSeed, FailureDiagnosis, MemoryHighlight,\n17\t    PlanEditBundle, RepoPlaybook, RulesDetector, ScenarioTraceBundle, SubsystemSummary, TaskBundle,\n18\t    WorkingSetContext,\n19\t};\n20\tuse lattice_core::memory::model::MemoryStructuredFields;\n21\tuse lattice_core::memory::{Memory, MemoryScope, MemoryStore, MemoryType};\n22\tuse lattice_core::query::{ContextCapsule, QueryEngine};\n23\tuse lattice_core::security::SecurityFilter;\n24\tuse lattice_core::storage::{GraphStore, SharedVectorIndex};\n25\tuse lattice_core::symbols::stable_file_handle;\n26\tuse lattice_core::watcher::should_index_file;\n27\tuse lattice_core::workspace::WorkspaceManager;\n28\t\n29\tuse super::context_cache::ContextHandleCache;\n30\tuse super::server::RequestHandler;\n31\tuse super::session_metrics::{SessionMetrics, SessionMetricsReport, ToolCallMetadata};\n32\t\n33\t/// MCP (Model Context Protocol) handler that routes JSON-RPC methods\n34\t/// to the appropriate tool implementations.\n35\tpub struct McpHandler {\n36\t    engine: Arc<Mutex<QueryEngine>>,\n37\t    indexer: Arc<Mutex<Indexer>>,\n38\t    memory_store: Arc<Mutex<MemoryStore>>,\n39\t    graph_store: Arc<Mutex<GraphStore>>,\n40\t    embedding_engine: Arc<OnceLock<Arc<EmbeddingEngine>>>,\n41\t    vector_index: Option<SharedVectorIndex>,\n42\t    workspace_root: PathBuf,\n43\t    session_id: String,\n44\t    #[allow(dead_code)]\n45\t    workspace_manager: Option<Arc<Mutex<WorkspaceManager>>>,\n46\t    workspace_roots: Vec<PathBuf>,\n47\t    indexing: Arc<AtomicBool>,\n48\t    context_cache: Arc<Mutex<ContextHandleCache>>,\n49\t    session_metrics: Arc<Mutex<SessionMetrics>>,\n50\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BbdQyD8DbWiNRxRFHe822D","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"b70ef4be-c228-4893-bf83-e09b9ec5ec2d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:18:28.127Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore extension + MCP surface"}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:141:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L2iJudk9QsMD8Akgmpbg1D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scenario Tracing\n2\t\n3\tPhase 4 adds a scenario-focused debugging workflow around `trace_scenario`. The goal is to take a behavior description and return the most likely execution paths first, without pretending that every plausible branch has been proven exhaustively.\n4\t\n5\t## Why This Exists\n6\t\n7\t`diagnose_failure` is still the right first call when you already have raw failure evidence such as a stack trace, compiler error, or failing test output. `trace_scenario` fills a different gap: the assistant has a behavior description and needs to reason about what code paths, guards, side effects, and failure branches are most relevant before it starts editing.\n8\t\n9\t## Contract\n10\t\n11\tThe workflow is exposed as an MCP tool with:\n12\t\n13\t- required `scenario`\n14\t- optional `entry_files` and `entry_symbols` to bias the search toward a known subsystem\n15\t- the usual workflow shaping controls: `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, and `render`\n16\t\n17\tThe bundle separates:\n18\t\n19\t- likely entrypoints from plausible alternatives\n20\t- the primary execution path from other plausible paths\n21\t- guard signals from side-effect signals\n22\t- failure branches from successful-path coverage\n23\t\n24\tThat separation matters. `likely` means the strongest evidence in the current graph and text signals, while `plausible` means the path is viable but lower confidence or weaker coverage. The bundle should be read as a prioritization aid, not as proof of full workspace coverage.\n25\t\n26\t## Follow-Up Behavior\n27\t\n28\tCompact responses can seed a `context_handle` for the trace result and expose a `suggested_expand` target focused on the most likely path. That keeps follow-up work anchored to the highest-signal branch first, while still allowing `expand_context` to widen the result when the assistant needs more depth.\n29\t\n30\tIf the caller already knows the likely subsystem, the optional entry-file or entry-symbol biasing should be used to improve ranking instead of forcing a broad workspace search.\n31\t\n32\t## Verification Scope\n33\t\n34\tThis note matches the landed core and daemon changes for `trace_scenario` and the focused regression coverage added with them. It does not claim full workspace validation or exhaustive behavioral proof.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgCYkkLu5MSqvwzg2iCDvg","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"13c71485-f2c0-45a7-a181-091536637296","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:18:28.429Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore docs and plans"}
