f files for a build harness. Do NOT implement the feature itself — just write the brief markdown files.\n\nRepo root: /home/pete/cadres/lattice\nSpec: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md  (READ Phases 8 and 9 sections + §MCP Surface especially \"Tool surface discipline\" + §Measurable Success Criteria + §Metrics And Evaluation)\nContext: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md\nTasks JSON: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks.json\nShared standards: /home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md\n\nWrite these 13 files at `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/<TASK_ID>.md`:\n\nT56, T57, T58, T59, T60, T61, T62, R63, R64, T65, T66, T67, T68, T69, R70\n\nThat's 15 files — write all of them.\n\n**Use the same template structure as prior agents**.\n\n**Task-specific guidance:**\n\n- T56 — redesigned `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`. Should compose graph + event + memory + working-memory substrates per spec §Phase 8 deliverables. One-call edit-planning bundles with code, docs, tests, memory, risks, verification commands.\n- T57 — redesigned `get_context_capsule`, `get_docs_capsule`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`. Compact-by-default with expansion handles.\n- T58 — new memory tools: `get_task_memory`, `save_memory`, `propose_memory_evolution` (unified with apply_memory_evolution per spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline\": consolidate `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` into one tool with `action` parameter).\n- T59 — new memory tools: `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` (unified per spec §MCP Surface discipline), `list_memory_conflicts`.\n- T60 — new tools: `consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`.\n- T61 — tool surface audit doc + final MCP reference. Required headings: `## Final tool list`, `#