attern extraction. MUST run only in background or manual-review modes, never on synchronous post-task hot path.\n- T43 — LLM provenance: each proposal records model, prompt hash, response hash. Queue depth bounded. Cost and latency budgets documented per job type in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md`. Failed/malformed responses leave prior memory unchanged and emit consolidation failure event.\n- T44 — manual review queue for high-scope (repo + organization) memory changes.\n- T45 — replay-safe execution: jobs can be replayed; provenance + prior state preserved.\n- T46 — integration tests: proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events.\n- R47 — Phase 6 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- T48 — verification engine core: file/symbol/doc/test existence checks. Outputs from spec §Verification Engine: verified/unverified/in_review/stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated.\n- T49 — exact-span evidence validation: when evidence captured an exact span, validate the span text still matches.\n- T50 — branch/workspace scope enforcement (deny leakage). Negative tests required.\n- T51 — time-bound expiry + incremental verification triggered by graph changes (large repos cannot tolerate full rescans).\n- T52 — stale surfacing in workflow bundles + label discipline: stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as trusted guidance. Non-negotiable from spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n- T53 — integration tests: stale never displayed as trusted; scope leakage blocked.\n- R54 — Phase 7 review. Required headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`.\n- R55 — contract gate Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval. Required headings: `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Stale-label round-trip`, `##