epo_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/concurrency_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/corruption_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/partial_index_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/workspace_boundary_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/migration_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs`\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-runbook.md`\n  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-recovery-playbook.md`\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy: `## Phase 11: Hardening`, `## Documentation Requirements`, `## Testing Requirements`, `## Storage Design` (event log compaction), `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`, `## Scope Leakage`.\n- Shared standards: `coding.md`, `definition-of-done-checklist.md`.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Open `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/` and confirm one module file per test family: `large_repo_tests.rs`, `concurrency_tests.rs`, `recovery_tests.rs`, `corruption_tests.rs`, `partial_index_tests.rs`, `workspace_boundary_tests.rs`, `migration_tests.rs`. Confirm `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs` exists.\n2. Run every Phase 11 test command end-to-end:\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::large_repo_tests -- --include-ignored`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::concurrency_tests -- --include-ignored`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::recovery_tests`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::corruption_tests`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::partial_index_tests`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::workspace_boundary_tests`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::migration_tests`\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::mcp_compat_tests`\n   - Capture pass/fail for each; any failure is a blocker.\n3. Open `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json` and confirm it contains entries for every hot path on every fixture; cross-check against T80's documented fixture list.\n4. Build the doc coverage matrix: list every item from spec §Documentation Requirements (eleven items), find the matching file produced by T85 (or, for the MCP contract reference, the T61 deliverable). Any unmapped item is a blocker.\n5. Open every doc from T85 and T86 and grep for required headings (the verification commands cover `## Overview`, `## Migration steps`, `## Daily operations`, `## Recovery procedures`, `## Replay from snapshot`); spot-check that the body content fills the heading promise rather than being a stub.\n6. Open the runbook and confirm the deploy sequence quoted matches `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy character-for-character: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`.\n7. Open the recovery playbook and confirm the replay-from-snapshot procedure cross-links to the T82 test that proves it works.\n8. Run `wc -l` on every Phase 11 artifact and confirm no file exceeds 800 lines per `coding.md`.\n9. Grep all Phase 11 artifacts for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, and unjustified suppressions — each hit is a blocker.\n10. Cross-check that the test families from spec §Testing Requirements are all present: storage migration, event append/replay, graph identity, parser, memory link, contradiction/supersession, stale verification, retrieval ranking golden, workflow golden, MCP schema, compact/full render, concurrency, large fixture performance, extension compile/UI smoke. The Phase 11 task set adds the hardening + migration + MCP compat coverage; earlier phases cover the remainder. Confirm every family has at least one passing test.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix for spec §Phase 11 deliverables (large-repo perf, concurrency, recovery, corrupted-event, partial-index, workspace-boundary, migration, MCP schema compatibility, documentation) and §Testing Requirements (every required test family). One row per deliverable, evidence column citing the artifact and the test/heading.\n- `## Doc coverage matrix` — one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements (eleven items). Columns: spec item, file delivered, file path, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK, notes.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. `coding.md` hard limits: file lengths (`wc -l` table for every Phase 11 file), forbidden-token grep results, suppression audit, tests-as-documentation audit (naming convention on every test function).\n- `## Hardening evidence` — for every Phase 11 test family, capture: command run, pass count, fail count, slow-test inclusion flag (`--include-ignored` for large_repo and concurrency), notable timings from `large_repo_results.json`, any P99 budget margin or breach.\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream gates can read it.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms spec alignment is a dedicated section.\n- `grep -q '## Doc coverage matrix' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms doc coverage matrix present.\n- `grep -q '## Coding-standard alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms standards audit performed.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms the review concludes with a binding verdict.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] `## Hardening evidence` and `## Findings` are also present (not gated by tasks.json verification but required for completeness).\n- [ ] Every Phase 11 test command was actually executed and the result captured under `## Hardening evidence`.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135377,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"e578665e-04f2-4831-94b5-3f5b4f5ed2de","request_id":"req_011Cb7Nnnq1PmkU6diUQFNyf","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
